DC Electrical Circuit Analysis — James M. Fiore (@pe-fiore-dc: 0, is #reference, #part-of @pe-sources) { r_4A9FXBXKNPS4JV50QQ3TVPS2GV
James M. Fiore. DC Electrical Circuit Analysis: A Practical Approach. [Author's complete book collection](https://www.jimfiore.org/Books.html) · [Author-hosted full text](https://www.jimfiore.org/books/DCElectricalCircuitAnalysis.pdf).

Read the entire book and work substantial analytical, design and practical exercises. It supplies a complete circuit foundation: quantities and components, sources and loads, network relations, theorems, nodal/mesh reasoning and time-dependent storage elements. Use its laboratory companion with suitable isolated educational apparatus and instruction.

The author offers these books as OER and the collection's licence link points to CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 Unported. Check the particular downloaded edition's notice and component exceptions; a host site's CC BY footer is not the book's licence. On 29 October 2026 the first automated retrieval identified 374 file pages, but repeated text retrieval timed out. Full-page inspection or a precise revision date is not claimed. No book, lab manual, figures or answers are bundled.

